+One-screen summary:
+• Adults-only boutique hotel (18+). Each booking has a check-in time, a check-out time and a list of accesses.
+• Registration form (FNRH) for every person, always. No form, no entry to the room.
+• Personal code. Never share your code or hold the gate for someone you don't know.
+• Visitors never enter rooms and are limited per day.
+• Quiet hours from 10 pm to 7 am. No parties.
+• Smoking only in the smoking area. No paid sexual services and no receiving clients.
+• Firearms only with a legal carry permit, notice before arrival and the hotel's OK.
+• Threats, violence or a conflict that brings in the police: everyone involved leaves.
+• Payment only through the stay link or the platform, in reais, no cash. The hotel does not charge fines: damage or cleaning beyond normal is charged at actual cost only, through the platform.
+• System failures are the hotel's fault, never the guest's. Emergencies: 192, 190, 193.
+
+0. WHAT A BOUTIQUE HOTEL MEANS TO US
+In Brazil there is no official category called "boutique hotel". In the market, the term refers to small, independent hotels with their own identity, few units and attention to each guest. It is not about luxury or room size: it is about small scale, personality and care.
+Why Dom Banana is a boutique hotel:
+• Independent: it does not belong to a hotel chain; it is a one-of-a-kind house with its own brand.
+• Small: just a few rooms, both private and shared.
+• Its own identity: the Dom Banana brand, the house's art and the neighborhood's culture are part of the stay.
+• Professional hospitality: active Cadastur, a registration form (FNRH) for every guest, public house rules, digital reception, incident records and management trained in support for women, LGBTQIA+ rights and health, disability, migration and health, and combating racial discrimination (Annex).
+• Technology serving the guest: personal door codes, a stay page, Wi-Fi and support in several languages.
+• Adapted for neurodivergent people: lots of texture, directional lighting, walls that avoid white and do not reflect light back into your eyes, spacious areas, sturdy furniture, corners to retreat to even in common areas and topfree use of the backyard. This is a rare kind of inclusion in Brazilian hospitality and as necessary as adaptation for mobility (section 13).
+
+1. WHO WE ARE AND HOW THESE RULES APPLY
+• Who we are: an independent boutique hotel, self-service, with no reception desk. Adults-only accommodation (18+).
+• Acknowledgement: these rules are in the listing before you book. By booking, you acknowledge them. There is no separate contract to sign.
+• A single source: the hotel's signs, books, TVs and messages only repeat what is written here. No new rule appears after booking.
+• Effective date: each version has a start date. The version that applies to your booking is the one in the listing on the day you booked.
+• Versions: the Core belongs to the network and changes only by network decision; each house has its own Annex, which completes the Core and never contradicts it. Every change is recorded in the Version History at the end.
+• Legal basis: the hotel follows Brazilian law and Airbnb's rules and does not repeat here what they already say. Whatever they prohibit remains prohibited at the hotel, even if not written down (section 16).
+• Official channel: the chat on the booking platform. Guests who booked directly with the hotel use the direct channel listed in the Annex.
+
+2. GLOSSARY
+• Pass: the check-in and check-out times and the list of accesses for each booking. The room is one of the accesses.
+• Unit: a private room (single or double), a bed in a mixed shared room, or an entire room.
+• Equivalent room: a room of the same type and with the same amenities as the one listed, assigned by the hotel at 2 pm on the day of arrival.
+• Private, common and outdoor areas: private areas are rooms, beds and bathrooms in use; common areas are the entrance, hallways, stairs, living room, kitchen and laundry; outdoor areas are the facade, sidewalk, porch, smoking area and backyard.
+• Camera, sensor and lock: a camera records images; a sensor does not record images (door, smoke, temperature, noise); the lock opens with a personal code.
+• Official channel: the chat on the booking platform, or the direct channel listed in the Annex.
+• @banana: a word that, when written in the official channel, calls a member of management right away.
+• Incident: any recorded fact that goes against these rules or puts someone at risk.
+• Those involved: the people who took part in a conflict. Anyone who only asked for help or witnessed it is not involved.
+
+3. CHECK-IN AND IDENTIFICATION
+• Who stays: only people on the booking may stay at the hotel, with a completed form and their own code, up to the number of guests in the listing. Extra guests must be requested as a booking change on the platform.
+• Registration form (FNRH): each guest fills in their own form through the link the hotel sends, before entering the room.
+• The form is never waived: if the system fails, the hotel immediately offers another way to complete the form (a new link or support by message), never entry without it. No one is left outside because of a system failure.
+• Codes: once all forms are complete, the codes are sent automatically. Returning guests at any house in the network only confirm their details.
+• Times: the Pass times are in the Annex. Entry is by code, at any time within the Pass hours.
+• Equivalent room: the booking guarantees the type of unit, not a specific room or bed. The hotel assigns the room at 2 pm on the day of arrival and sends the number through the booking messages.
+• Early check-in and late check-out: requested through the official channel, subject to availability, up to the limit in the Annex, and charged through the platform itself, with the price shown before you accept.
+• Someone you don't recognize: do not confront them. Write @banana in the official channel; if in danger, call 190. The hotel checks who is staying and who opened the doors at that time. Anyone unregistered is invited to register through the platform or to leave; if they refuse or there is a risk: platform Safety team and 190.
+
+4. LIVING TOGETHER
+• Quiet: during the hours in the Annex, keep voices low and make no noise, including inside the room. Music and videos in common areas only with headphones, except at hotel events.
+• Parties: prohibited. Events only when organized and announced by the hotel.
+• Alcohol: allowed in moderation in common areas until quiet hours begin. Drunkenness that disturbs, intimidates or threatens others is serious misconduct.
+• Smoking: only in the smoking area listed in the Annex, vaping included.
+• Animals: the hotel does not accept pets.
+• Mixed shared rooms: when possible, the hotel places guests of the same gender in the same room, with no guarantee. Shared rooms are for sleeping only; no intimate activity there.
+• Bathrooms: shared and gender-neutral. Hair removal, haircuts and hair dyeing are prohibited.
+• Work and commerce: remote work in common areas is allowed, with headphones. Selling, giving paid lessons, seeing clients or taking commercial photos and videos at the hotel only with the hotel's prior authorization.
+• Conversations: politics, religion, culture and sexuality are open topics, with respect.
+
+5. VISITORS
+• Where: visitors never enter rooms, private or shared. They stay only in common areas, during the visiting hours in the Annex, and do not sleep at the hotel.
+• Notice: each visit is announced in advance through the official channel, with the visitor's name. The hotel may ask for ID on arrival.
+• Limit per booking: 1 visitor at a time and at most 2 different visitors per day, even if one leaves before the other arrives.
+• Services disguised as visits: back-to-back visits by different people for services (paid service, session, arranged meeting) are treated as a prohibited service (section 11).
+• Visitor Pass: visits of up to 1 hour are free. Beyond that, the Pass in the Annex is optional, paid through the stay link, and the amount becomes credit to spend at the house shop.
+
+6. TOPFREE BACKYARD AND POOL
+• Topfree: in the backyard, swimwear bottoms are mandatory for everyone. Tops are optional for anyone, regardless of gender, identity or body, including bodies with surgical scars, such as from a mastectomy.
+• Not a nudist area: adults over 18 only, with no sexual connotation and no photographing or filming other people.
+• Privacy: the backyard has no camera and cannot be seen from the street. Outside it: clothing or a towel. On the street, always clothed.
+• Intimacy: no sexual activity in the presence of others, in any common area.
+• Pool (when open): no swimming alone, at night or after drinking, and no diving headfirst. The hotel has no lifeguard.
+
+7. CAMERAS, SENSORS AND YOUR DATA
+• Security cameras: visible and signposted, only in outdoor areas and in the common circulation areas listed in the Annex, with the location of each one. Never in rooms, beds, bathrooms or the backyard. No audio and no facial recognition. Every camera is disclosed in the listing.
+• Footage: viewed only by hotel management, when there is an incident. It may be handed to the platform and to the authorities. It is kept for the period in the Annex; in an incident, until the case is closed.
+• Sensors: door, smoke and temperature. A noise sensor, if any, only in a common area and disclosed in the Annex.
+• Wi-Fi: access is with the stay password (Annex). The hotel keeps the connection log for 1 year, without keeping what you browse.
+• Your data, what it is for and how long it is kept:
+• Registration form (FNRH): guest registry; for the legal period.
+• Photo of your ID: to check the form details; deleted after checking.
+• Selfie: to confirm the person is the owner of the ID; low quality, for identification only, for the same period as the form.
+• Contact details: support and sending codes; for as long as the relationship with the hotel lasts.
+• Lock logs: security and investigation of incidents; up to 1 year, in a separate log on the hotel's server; in an incident, until the case is closed.
+• Wi-Fi connection log: legal requirement; 1 year.
+• Purchases and extras: billing and invoicing; for the tax period.
+• Messages with the hotel: support; for as long as the relationship with the hotel lasts.
+• Camera footage: security; for the period in the Annex.
